  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#actualFrameShearArea">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Actual frame shear area</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <skos:altLabel>actual_frame_shear_area</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for actualFrameShearArea derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Actual frame shear area</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0006</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The section modulus of a longitudinal frame shall be calculated using Z = f_4*p*h*l^2/(4*m*sigma_y)*10^6 [cm^3] (4.9). The effective shear area shall be A = sqrt(3)*f_4*f_5*p*h*l/(2*sigma_y)*10^4 [cm^2] (4.10). The bracket shear area shall not be included in the actual frame shear area. Use f_4 = 1 - 0.2*h/s, f_5 = 2.16, p from 4.2.2, h from 4.2.1, s as fram...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#moduleHull"/>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>Area</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
