    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for safetyFactorFatigue derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Safety factor fatigue</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0643</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>At every blade location, the equivalent fatigue stress shall satisfy sigma_fl/sigma_fat &gt;= 1.5 (6.45). Use sigma_fl = gamma_e1*gamma_e2*gamma_v*gamma_m*sigma_exp. If actual reduction factors are unavailable, use gamma_e1*gamma_e2 = 0.67, gamma_v = 0.75 and gamma_m = 0.75. Blade bolts, CP mechanism, propeller boss and propeller-shaft fitting shall have safety...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>DimensionlessRatio</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>safetyFactorFatigue</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>safety_factor_fatigue</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-110 | TRAFICOM p.51 | 6.6.2.4; 6.6.3</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-110</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>safetyFactorFatigue</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical dimensionless unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>1</nltl:unitSymbol>
  </rdf:Description>
