    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Delta is the displacement of the ship at a maximum ice class draught [t] (see section 2.2). P is the actual continuous engine output of the ship [kW] (see section 3.1) available when sailing in ice. If additional power sources are available for propulsion power (e.g. shaft motors) in addition to the power of the main engine(s), they shall also be included in...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
