  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#weatherProtectionPresent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Weather protection present</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
    <skos:altLabel>weather_protection_present</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for weatherProtectionPresent derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Weather protection present</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0809</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Taking into account the presence of any hazards, as identified in the assessment in chapter 1, resources shall be provided to support survival following abandoning ship, whether to the water, to ice or to land, for the maximum expected time of rescue. These resources shall provide: a habitable environment; protection of persons from the effects of cold, wind...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Locked-workbook normalized regulatory term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N4 - preserve the source concept; normalize spelling to ASCII lowerCamelCase</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Stage 1 explicit boolean</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>weather_protection_present</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceReference>IMO-065 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.23-24 | 8.2.3.3</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>IMO-065</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>weatherProtectionPresent</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Not a quantity property</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#actualWebFrameCrossSectionalArea">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Actual web-frame cross-sectional area</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <skos:altLabel>A_a_cm2</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for actualShearArea derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Actual web-frame cross-sectional area</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0007</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The section modulus of a web frame shall be calculated using Z = (M/sigma_y)*sqrt(1/(1 - (gamma*A/A_a)^2))*10^6 [cm^3] (4.17), where M is the maximum calculated bending moment under ice load F and shall be M = 0.193*F*L, gamma is selected from Table 4-8, A is the required shear area, and A_a = A_f + A_w is the actual cross-sectional area of the web frame.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#moduleHull"/>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>Area</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM2"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>A_a_cm2</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-060 | TRAFICOM p.24 | 4.6.2</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-060</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>actualShearArea</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:stage2UnitEvidence>TRF-060 explicitly gives [cm^2]</nltl:stage2UnitEvidence>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>cm^2</nltl:unitSymbol>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#certificateLanguage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Certificate language</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <skos:altLabel>certificate_language</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for certificateLanguage derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Certificate language</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0127</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The Polar Ship Certificate shall be drawn up in a form corresponding to the model given in appendix I to this Code. If the language used is neither English, nor French or Spanish, the text shall include a translation into one of these languages.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#moduleDocuments"/>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Locked-workbook normalized regulatory term</nltl:namingBasis>
