    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0193</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>An ice-strengthened ship is assumed to operate in open sea conditions corresponding to a level ice thickness not exceeding hi. The design ice load height (h) of the area actually under ice pressure at any particular point of time is, however, assumed to be only a fraction of the ice thickness. The values for hi and h are given in Table 4-1.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
