    <skos:altLabel>LBOW</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for bowLength derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Bow length</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0101</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>(ii) The waterline length of the bow region is generally to be divided into 4 sub-regions of equal length. The force (F), line load (Q), pressure (P) and load patch aspect ratio (AR) are to be calculated with respect to the mid-length position of each sub-region (each maximum of F, Q and P is to be used in the calculation of the ice load parameters Pavg, b a...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
