  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#peakPressureFactor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Peak pressure factor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <skos:altLabel>peakPressureFactor</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for peakPressureFactor derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Peak pressure factor</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0530</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>(i) The average pressure, Pavg, within a design load patch is determined as follows: Pavg = F / (b * w) [MPa] where F = FBow or FNonBow as appropriate for the hull area under consideration [MN] b = bBow or bNonBow as appropriate for the hull area under consideration [m] w = wBow or wNonBow as appropriate for the hull area under consideration [m] (ii) Areas o...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl-benchmark/vocab#moduleHull"/>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>DimensionlessRatio</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>peakPressureFactor</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceReference>I2-018 | IACS_UR_I2 p.7 | I2.3.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>I2-018</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>peakPressureFactor</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical dimensionless unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>1</nltl:unitSymbol>
  </rdf:Description>
